 byte-identical to the candidate (`f926d104…`, verified three times across the mutant runs).\n\n## The one blocking finding\n\nАхпер джан, G-A was the right place to look — the sweep is real, but its pair dimension is not derived.\n\n`surrogate_test.go` says \"Dimensions, each fully enumerated\" and \"a narrowed bound diverges from the oracle on every vector it newly admits\". The second unit of a pair is a hand-written five-element list:\n\n```go\nfor _, second := range []int{0xdc00, 0xdc01, 0xdfff, 0x0041, 0xd800} {\n```\n\nBoth values adjacent to the low-surrogate range are missing — `0xdbff` below, `0xe000` above. They're the only seconds that separate the correct bound from an off-by-one, so both narrowings survive the **whole** provhost package:\n\n| mutant | `surrogate.go:71` | result |\n| --- | --- | ---: |\n| `SGC` | `low > 0xe000` | **SURVIVED** |\n| `SGJ` | `low < 0xdbff` | **SURVIVED** |\n\nReal production divergence, probed directly: under `SGC`, `decodeStrictObject` accepts `{\"a\":\"\\ud800\\ue000\"}` while `canonicaljson` refuses it — a lone high surrogate reaching `encoding/json` to become U+FFFD, the exact Section 1.6 class. 239,630 swept vectors say nothing about it. `repeat-of: revision 5 / F2` — second consecutive same-class finding, so the fix must derive the dimension from the gate's own range constants, not extend the list by two.\n\n## Everything else measured clean\n\n- **Round-7 F2 closed**: `SG1`/`SG5` now KILLED; escape-unit, hex-case, raw-UTF-8 dimensions genuinely enumerated. Five other narrowings I planted all killed.\n- **F3 pinned**: `F3b-peekOnlyMajorAbove3` KILLED by `TestDecodeResponseForeignMajorPrecedesMemberRules`.\n- **F1 deadline fix pinned**: `RN8-collectDrainsUnbounded` KILLED at 20.23s.\n- **G-B**: registry re-pin is computed, not copied; fails closed 3/3 (forged row, repointed declaration, one-word gap-prose edit → digest mismatch). All 14 named declarations exist. All four false gap texts rewritten.\n- **G-C**: all three advisories answered in the tree.\n- **G-D**: 177 rows across 16 batteries, **zero resurrections**. Every round-7 `NOT_APPLIED` anchor re-anchored rather than counted as a pass. `internal/provider` subtree byte-identical (`b1f62223`) so leaf 1 can't resurrect — measured, not assumed.\n- Gates: build/vet/windows-vet/gofmt clean, 15 packages green, provhost `-count=8` and `-race` green, coverage 85.8/97.0/86.6%.\n\nTwo advisories recorded, not blocking: `RN1`/`RN2` (the `writeErr` ordering half of round-6 F2) still unpinned, carried from round 7; and the `Process.Kill` backstop branch is unreachable on unix — `Setpgid` makes the direct child a group leader so its own `setsid()` fails EPERM — with `RN4`/`RN6`/`RN7`/`RN9` all surviving and the justifying comment naming a scenario the code structurally prevents.\n\nArtifacts on the board: `TASK-260830-32jeti_review-verdict-round8.md` and `TASK-260830-32jeti_review-round8-probe-pack.tgz` (harness, all 16 battery logs, `reanchor.json` with `SGC`/`SGJ`, two drop-in probes).","ttft_ms":2368,"type":"result","duration_ms":3095524,"uuid":"b3f72ef4-9a9c-4a81-9620-196cca70b8fb","ttft_stream_ms":1857,"time_to_request_ms":19,"first_content_frame_ms":1857,"queued_turn_count":0}
